// =============================================================================
// cli -- the tethernet-cli command line
// =============================================================================

// The CLI help text lives here as whole sentences rather than split into tiny pieces:
// the text must align as fixed layout, and dozens of tiny strings cannot keep the widths consistent.
TETHERNET_MESSAGE(kCliUsage, "Usage: sudo tethernet-cli [options]\n"
    "\n"
    "  A user-space RNDIS driver for macOS: turns an RNDIS device (Android USB\n"
    "  tethering and friends) into an interface the system can see.\n"
    "\n"
    "Device selection:\n"
    "  --vid <hex>           only match this USB vendor ID (e.g. 18d1)\n"
    "  --pid <hex>           only match this USB product ID (e.g. 4ee4)\n"
    "  --list                list the RNDIS devices found and exit (**no root needed**)\n"
    "\n"
    "Interface:\n"
    "  --mtu <bytes>         desired MTU, default 1500 (lowered automatically if the\n"
    "                        device cannot carry it; capped by sysctl\n"
    "                        net.link.fake.max_mtu)\n"
    "  --keep-feth-mac       do not set the system-side MAC to the address the device\n"
    "                        reports\n"
    "\n"
    "Performance tuning:\n"
    "  --rx-transfers <n>    bulk IN transfers in flight, default 16\n"
    "  --tx-transfers <n>    bulk OUT transfers in flight, default 4. Measured 4/8/16\n"
    "                        with no discernible difference (a full pool waits for a\n"
    "                        slot instead of dropping frames), so you rarely need this\n"
    "  --rx-transfer-kb <n>  KiB per bulk IN buffer, default 16\n"
    "  --max-transfer-kb <n> MaxTransferSize announced in INITIALIZE (KiB), default 16.\n"
    "                        This is the only way to make the device aggregate packets\n"
    "                        and is the main throughput lever; larger is usually faster\n"
    "  --max-tx-packets <n>  how many RNDIS packets to aggregate per host -> device\n"
    "                        transfer. 0 (default) means honour the device's reported\n"
    "                        MaxPacketsPerMessage. Diagnostic: if you suspect the device\n"
    "                        claims aggregation but only unpacks the first packet, set 1\n"
    "                        and compare. Note that aggregation worked on every Android\n"
    "                        device tested and clamping to 1 was slower -- do not reach\n"
    "                        for this as a default cure for dropped frames\n"
    "  --bpf-buffer-kb <n>   KiB for the BPF kernel capture buffer, default 4096\n"
    "\n"
    "Other:\n"
    "  --stats <ms>          statistics reporting interval, 0 disables, default 5000\n"
    "  --log <level>         trace|debug|info|warn|error|off, default info\n"
    "  --lang <language>     interface language, default auto -- checks\n"
    "                        TETHERNET_LANG, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES and LANG in that order\n"
    "                        and takes the first non-empty value. English is the only\n"
    "                        language shipped today; en and auto both select it. sudo\n"
    "                        does not always pass those through, so pass --lang\n"
    "                        explicitly then\n"
    "  --no-color            disable coloured log output\n"
    "  -h, --help            show this help\n"
    "  -V, --version         show the version\n"
    "\n"
    "Why root is required: creating the feth virtual interface and opening /dev/bpf*\n"
    "both need root. The USB side does not -- macOS ships no RNDIS kernel driver, so\n"
    "libusb can claim the interface directly.\n")

